{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975787,"nonce":"hwaHeLtiDHi3tUBhsHc2pg70rwE=","title":"AIR needs loop vectorization for the Cranelift tier","message":"Deferring vectorization to LLVM assumed LLVM was the only compiled backend.\nCranelift has SIMD types and instructions (`i8x16`..`f64x2`, including a vector\n`fma`) and NO vectorizing pass, so whatever the middle tier should vectorize, AIR\nmust vectorize.\n\nPrerequisites mostly exist: alias classes give memory dependence, loop analysis\ngives trip structure. Still needed are unit-stride access detection over\nvarray/Bytes data and a cost model. Best targets are Bytes/varray loops (clean\nstride, no cross-class aliasing) and pixel loops once inlining and scalar\nreplacement have de-abstracted them.","files":null}]}